# Custom domain for GitHub Pages.
# Replace this file with your actual domain. GitHub Pages will serve the
# site at https://<your-domain> (instead of https://<user>.github.io/<repo>/).
#
# Setup steps:
# 1. Put your domain here, e.g.  docs.lodestone.dev
# 2. Commit + push to the branch GitHub Pages publishes from (master)
# 3. In repo Settings → Pages → Custom domain → enter the same domain → Save
# 4. At your DNS registrar, add a CNAME record:
#      <your-subdomain>.CNAME <user>.github.io.
#    (or apex domain: add A records 185.199.108.153 / .154 / .155 / .156)
# 5. Wait ~1 min for DNS + GitHub Pages to issue a Let's Encrypt cert
# 6. Settings → Pages → "Enforce HTTPS" → tick
#
# Without this file, GitHub Pages serves at https://<user>.github.io/<repo>/
docs.lodestone.dev
